# Proponents of "Multicultural" Humanities Research Call for a Critical Look at Its Achievements.

**Authors:** Winkler, Karen J.

## Abstract
Multicultural scholarship was critiqued by proponents at a meeting of the American Studies Association for a "politics of style" substituting for analysis of society; a "particularism" that has divided researchers into separate camps; and a "political correctness" that has avoided self-criticism. One issue raised was that multiculturalism further marginalizes minority groups. (DB)

